# The website needs no environment variables to build or serve its pages.
# /api/star-history.svg reads GITHUB_TOKEN, a Cloudflare Worker secret
# (npx wrangler secret put GITHUB_TOKEN); without it the chart serves its
# fallback card. For local runs, put it in .dev.vars, which git ignores.
# Scowld Premium (/api/live, /api/premium/balance) needs two more Worker
# secrets: GEMINI_API_KEY (Scowld's own Gemini key) and REVENUECAT_SECRET_KEY
# (a RevenueCat API v2 key with customer information read access only). Without
# them Premium answers "unavailable". For a local end-to-end test, .dev.vars can
# also set REVENUECAT_API_BASE to a stand-in for RevenueCat's API.
# Users' own provider keys are entered inside the iOS app and stored in the iOS Keychain.
